{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChU1aE97NeW6y8nZJWYad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`ard init --pr` now accepts the same credentials as `ard serve` for a live run: a GitHub App, `ARD_GITHUB_TOKEN`, or the `gh` CLI fallback, which is held in memory. `go vet` and `go test` on `./internal/initcmd` pass. A run of `go test ./internal/...` hit my 2-minute tool timeout, so I didn't see its full result.\n\n- **Code:** `internal/initcmd/initcmd.go` has a new `resolveAuth` that mirrors serve's, and `checkAuth` is gone. `--dry-run` behaves as before.\n- **PR body:** `internal/initcmd/body.go` now takes the auth kind. The last section is \"Follow-up ard does not do\" and says ard never writes `.github/`. For an App it says the App lacks permission. For a token it says the token may be able to write `.github/` but ard still doesn't, and that the bot-commit check can't tell ard's commits from the token user's.\n- **Tests:** I added `TestResolveAuth` and `TestInitBodyAuthKinds`, which cover the App, token and gh cases. I didn't add a live `--pr` run with a token-kind identity, because the existing test harness bypasses auth selection.\n- **Docs:** `docs/runbooks/onboard-repo.md` and `docs/proposal.md` now say init works with either auth. `docs/site/getting-started.md` and `docs/layout.md` had no App-only wording, so I left them alone.\n\nThe report is at `.ard/458/worker-engineer.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":776,"cache_read_input_tokens":33787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":776},"output_tokens":521,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"722ce48d-201b-495f-b707-ef0110c1be2a","uuid":"3d6ae9b2-f23a-4f8d-85e4